WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:29.960
CIBC shares sit 7% below the $1.7050 fair value mark after a $1 billion note sale. This is Modern Investing Techniques, Episode 207. After the close, we screen Canadian AI names, walk a simulated 5-session bank hold, review Eritzia, then options flow tools, the open book, and a covered call you can run in a TFSA. Quick reminder, everything we discuss here is for education and entertainment. The practice investment of the day uses simulated trades with

00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:35.680
no real money. I'm not a licensed financial advisor, and this isn't financial advice. Always

00:00:35.680 --> 00:00:40.656
do your own research before putting real money to work. Economists are lifting the odds

00:00:40.656 --> 00:00:45.856
of a bank of Canada hike as inflation stays stubborn, and that is the macro sitting on every

00:00:45.856 --> 00:00:54.816
Canadian bank name tonight. The S&amp;P 500 closed at 7,713, up 3 tens of a percent, while the NASDAQ

00:00:54.816 --> 00:00:59.376
composite finished at 26,425, flat on the session.

00:00:59.996 --> 00:01:07.376
That NASDAQ print is up 13.73% year to date, and up 18.10% since the practice portfolio

00:01:07.376 --> 00:01:09.916
opened on March 16th, 2026.

00:01:10.716 --> 00:01:17.676
The TSX composite closed at 36,108, up half a percent, with financials leading the tape

00:01:17.676 --> 00:01:20.156
and energy lagging even as oil moved higher.

00:01:20.156 --> 00:01:25.476
market still price a hold from the Bank of Canada on October 29th and from the

00:01:25.476 --> 00:01:30.316
Federal Reserve later in the year, so the Hike Talk is a change in odds, not a

00:01:30.316 --> 00:01:36.017
decision already in the bag. About 14 days ago we simulated AMD on a Samsung

00:01:36.017 --> 00:01:42.517
semiconductor partnership catalyst, and that name closed down 4.61%, which is why I

00:01:42.517 --> 00:01:47.557
am slower to size a catalyst until the sector tape agrees. Thematic investing in

00:01:47.557 --> 00:01:52.317
Canadian AI names paid when investors screened for companies already posting revenue growth

00:01:52.317 --> 00:01:56.237
above 30% and trading at reasonable multiples to that growth.

00:01:56.737 --> 00:02:01.957
The method is simple, find sector leadership in an emerging theme, then confirm those names

00:02:01.957 --> 00:02:06.417
have already beaten the TSX by a wide margin before you add a dollar of exposure.

00:02:07.077 --> 00:02:13.997
Two Canadian AI holdings have locked in gains of 78% and 71% while the broader index lagged,

00:02:13.997 --> 00:02:18.757
which is the edge from identifying the theme early rather than chasing it once it is obvious.

00:02:19.497 --> 00:02:27.277
Implementation starts with a screen on investing.com, Canada, or your broker's sector ETF list for AI or software holdings,

00:02:27.437 --> 00:02:32.057
then a cross-check of year-to-date performance and revenue growth from the latest filings.

00:02:32.637 --> 00:02:41.477
Historically, this has worked best in the first 18-24 months of a new technology cycle, when earnings visibility is still expanding rather than rolling over.

00:02:41.477 --> 00:02:47.157
Prior tech cycles show that names beating the TSX by more than 50% in the first year

00:02:47.157 --> 00:02:53.157
of a theme often keep outperforming for another 12 months if revenue growth stays above 25%.

00:02:53.557 --> 00:02:58.637
The risks are real, the theme can rotate out quickly once growth rates peak, or when

00:02:58.637 --> 00:03:03.157
broader market volatility rises and high multiple software is the first thing sold.

00:03:03.737 --> 00:03:10.177
One practical step is to put no more than 5% of a tax-free savings account, or TFSA, into

00:03:10.177 --> 00:03:14.797
any single thematic name and rebalance quarterly with the same revenue growth and relative

00:03:14.797 --> 00:03:15.777
performance filters.

00:03:16.537 --> 00:03:21.497
On wealth simple or quest trade, and I have no financial relationship with either, you

00:03:21.497 --> 00:03:26.377
can build a custom watch list that flags software and semiconductor names whose 20-day average

00:03:26.377 --> 00:03:29.377
volume sits above their 50-day average before you enter.

00:03:30.157 --> 00:03:34.817
That volume filter is how those two stand out Canadian AI holdings separated themselves

00:03:34.817 --> 00:03:36.377
on the initial breakout days.

00:03:36.377 --> 00:03:41.613
week or names that later faded never cleared it. Canadian Imperial Bank of

00:03:41.613 --> 00:03:47.293
Commerce ticker CM on the TSX is the simulated weekly hold and this is a

00:03:47.293 --> 00:03:51.893
simulated trade for learning purposes with no real money attached. The entry is

00:03:51.893 --> 00:03:57.613
159 Canadian dollars and 12 cents. A valuation gap against the consensus mark we

00:03:57.613 --> 00:04:06.053
opened on with 20-day average volume still supportive on the recent advance. Two

00:04:06.053 --> 00:04:12.893
common equity tier 1 ratio of 13.4%, plus a 26% year-to-date share price gain that

00:04:12.893 --> 00:04:18.943
says momentum has not rolled over. Yahoo Finance also shows active share repurchase programs

00:04:18.943 --> 00:04:24.483
covering up to 3% of shares, which can support earnings per share even if loan growth slows,

00:04:24.883 --> 00:04:32.923
and a 3-year total shareholder return of 273.21%. The long-dated notes do 2086 sit as fixed

00:04:32.923 --> 00:04:37.743
to floating paper, so the coupon can adjust if rates move, which is why the capital

00:04:37.743 --> 00:04:44.465
raise did not automatically kill the valuation case. Target is plus 4% to 7% over 5 sessions

00:04:44.465 --> 00:04:50.745
if that valuation gap narrows. The stop sits at the 50-day moving average near $152.8.

00:04:51.785 --> 00:04:57.425
Confidence is medium, two factors aligned, but sector rotation into banks is not yet confirmed

00:04:57.425 --> 00:05:02.345
by volume, and I am not going to pretend the leadership print on the TSX is the same

00:05:02.345 --> 00:05:03.905
thing as a volume confirmation.

00:05:04.745 --> 00:05:09.645
Eritzia just paid us for respecting catalysts and still left size on the table because consumer

00:05:09.645 --> 00:05:12.325
discretionary rotation was never confirmed first.

00:05:12.985 --> 00:05:17.605
That is why this bank entry stays medium and does not get a full-size allocation until

00:05:17.605 --> 00:05:18.805
the volume filter clears.

00:05:19.525 --> 00:05:21.445
In validation is the habit to copy.

00:05:22.045 --> 00:05:25.545
The most followed fair value estimate falls below the current share price.

00:05:26.125 --> 00:05:30.545
If that data point moves, the thesis is done, no debating, no averaging down.

00:05:31.185 --> 00:05:35.905
Primary risk remains a deeper housing slowdown or higher for longer rates, pressuring

00:05:35.905 --> 00:05:36.605
loan growth.

00:05:37.025 --> 00:05:42.185
We hold five sessions from entry and evaluate on Friday unless that invalidation or the moving

00:05:42.185 --> 00:05:43.585
average stop hits first.

00:05:44.618 --> 00:05:51.038
Eritzia, ticker ATZ on the TSX, was the last weekly hold, evaluation entry after an earnings

00:05:51.038 --> 00:05:52.798
beat, and a guidance lift.

00:05:53.238 --> 00:05:59.578
We simulated buying at $143 Canadian dollars and 36 cents on the Tuesday open and exited

00:05:59.578 --> 00:06:06.038
at 150 Canadian dollars and 38 cents on the Monday close, a six-calendar day window. That

00:06:06.038 --> 00:06:15.058
is a gain of 4.90% or $48.97 on a $1,000 simulated position. Over the same window, the NASDAQ

00:06:15.058 --> 00:06:22.378
gained roughly 1.8%, so the trade produced 3.1% of alpha, a win against the benchmark, not just a

00:06:22.378 --> 00:06:27.758
green number. The earnings catalyst did the work. The gain would have been larger if sector rotation

00:06:27.758 --> 00:06:31.298
into consumer discretionary had been confirmed before we sized it.

00:06:31.738 --> 00:06:37.038
Rule, cross-check sector rotation signals before sizing earnings driven entries in retail names.

00:06:38.051 --> 00:06:40.871
Unusual Wales is a real-time options flow feed

00:06:40.871 --> 00:06:44.611
that surfaces large trades before the move shows up in the share price,

00:06:45.191 --> 00:06:47.671
and I have no financial relationship with the platform.

00:06:48.271 --> 00:06:51.911
Canadian investors can use the free tier to monitor TSX names

00:06:51.911 --> 00:06:54.531
and the paid tier for deeper filters and alerts,

00:06:55.071 --> 00:06:57.551
which is most useful if you already have a short list

00:06:57.551 --> 00:06:59.191
rather than hunting the whole market.

00:06:59.791 --> 00:07:03.211
Set alerts for flow exceeding 500 contracts on a single strike.

00:07:03.651 --> 00:07:06.871
That size often precedes headline moves in high beta names.

00:07:07.491 --> 00:07:12.551
The feed also flags unusual whale activity in names such as Tesla and SpaceX when merger

00:07:12.551 --> 00:07:18.351
related committees form, which is early visibility into a volatility spike, not a buy signal

00:07:18.351 --> 00:07:18.931
by itself.

00:07:19.611 --> 00:07:24.471
Alerts can push into wealth simple or interactive brokers watch lists through broker APIs,

00:07:24.471 --> 00:07:26.951
size, so you are not sitting on the feed all day.

00:07:28.022 --> 00:07:29.822
Endbridge is the income math homework.

00:07:30.222 --> 00:07:34.882
The full walks how many shares you would need at the current price to earn $1,000 of

00:07:34.882 --> 00:07:39.402
dividend income each year, then asks you to compare the payout ratio with peers.

00:07:40.082 --> 00:07:44.482
Pipeline volumes recovering and possible future payout growth make that position-size

00:07:44.482 --> 00:07:50.242
calculation especially relevant for TFSA holders who already treat the name as a yield anchor.

00:07:50.242 --> 00:07:56.308
CBC describes the Canadian housing market as on its knees, with stubborn inflation pushing

00:07:56.308 --> 00:08:00.488
some economists to price a possible rate hike next week for the first time since the

00:08:00.488 --> 00:08:03.268
Bank of Canada last raised in July 2023.

00:08:03.988 --> 00:08:09.548
An 8th consecutive hold is still widely predicted, but the action is to review any variable rate

00:08:09.548 --> 00:08:14.848
debt you carry and model the cash flow hit of a 25 basis point increase before that decision

00:08:14.848 --> 00:08:15.168
lands.

00:08:16.118 --> 00:08:21.378
ARRI's Capital, the business development company, trades below net asset value with a high

00:08:21.378 --> 00:08:25.938
yield attached, and the Fools read is to wait for the upcoming earnings report rather

00:08:25.938 --> 00:08:27.318
than buy the discount blind.

00:08:27.938 --> 00:08:32.378
Compare that discount with the five-year average and let credit quality trends on the print

00:08:32.378 --> 00:08:34.978
tell you whether the gap compresses or widens.

00:08:35.518 --> 00:08:41.538
The simulated book runs $1,000 per trade under rules published on August 18, 2026.

00:08:41.538 --> 00:08:48.138
Fixed five session holds, entry at the next open, stop or horizon exits, and no discretionary

00:08:48.138 --> 00:08:52.958
early sales. Those rules are the product. You should be able to take the pick, the date,

00:08:53.218 --> 00:08:58.598
and the stop and reproduce every number we report. Earlier trades remain on the site as history,

00:08:59.098 --> 00:09:02.698
but they were exited on whatever day the evaluating run happened to price,

00:09:03.198 --> 00:09:08.558
so they cannot tell you whether this method beats the index. Across 33 rules-based trades,

00:09:08.558 --> 00:09:16.318
rates, matched window alpha versus the NASDAQ sits at minus 31.55%, across 84 total simulated

00:09:16.318 --> 00:09:23.938
trades, the win rate is 52%. 44 wins, 39 losses, 1 break even, with cumulative P&amp;L of

00:09:23.938 --> 00:09:33.978
minus $27.15, an average return of minus 0.03%, a best trade of plus 20.11%, a worst of

00:09:33.978 --> 00:09:38.198
minus 27.14%, and a current streak of 4 wins.

00:09:38.818 --> 00:09:42.398
Year-to-date, the simulated book is minus 0.03%

00:09:42.398 --> 00:09:46.398
against the NASDAQ composite at plus 13.73%.

00:09:46.788 --> 00:09:49.698
That buy-and-hold gap is why we measure matched windows

00:09:49.698 --> 00:09:51.018
instead of just the calendar.

00:09:51.718 --> 00:09:56.838
Open positions are ENB on the TSX, BN on the TSX and GM,

